WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.640
You’re a researcher working at Site-19 for
the SCP Foundation, just going about your

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.080
day, minding your own business.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.580
You’ve spent your morning keeping an eye
on the D-classes who are keeping their eyes

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.270
on SCP-173, while also.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.900
The clock strikes noon, and you decide to
break for lunch, where you’ll enjoy the

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.220
delicious tuna sandwich you made for yourself
this morning.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:28.310
You’re sitting alone in one of Site-19’s
numerous employee break rooms, chewing the

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.800
first bite of your sandwich as you try in
vain to wrap your head around SCP-055, the

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.680
unknowable Anti-Meme, when a scent wafts past
your nose.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.160
It’s the worst thing you’ve ever smelled,
like a mix of body odor, dirt, and musty,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.640
old clothes.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:50.140
You turn to look for the source of the smell,
and suddenly realize that you’re not alone

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:51.140
in the room.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:56.630
There’s a man standing next to you - he’s
tall, with a scruffy face lined by age.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:00.489
He’s wearing a long woolen coat that dangles
past his knees.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:07.579
He doesn’t say a word though, he’s just
staring - but not at you, at your sandwich.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:12.039
Before you can open your tuna filled mouth
to say something, his greatcoat opens, and

00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:17.380
a long, green tentacle slithers out, grabbing
your sandwich and pulling it out of your hands.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:22.689
You start to protest, and then another limb
emerges from the coat, long and reptilian.

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:26.920
It places a single finger up to your lips
and shushes you.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.359
The tentacle lifts your delicious tuna sandwich
up to the strange man’s face, and he starts

00:01:31.359 --> 00:01:36.009
to eat it in front of you, maintaining eye
contact the entire time.

00:01:36.009 --> 00:01:41.619
Then, after he finishes your lunch, he just
turns and makes his exit, leaving you alone

00:01:41.619 --> 00:01:44.079
in the breakroom… and hungry.

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:48.590
Later that day, you request a meeting with
your supervisor, hoping to get some answers

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:54.189
about what you saw in the breakroom, maybe
some compensation for the stolen sandwich,

00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:59.399
or at the very least, a little sympathy for
how hungry you’ve been all afternoon.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:02.429
But your supervisor does none of that.

00:02:02.429 --> 00:02:06.090
Instead the color drains from their cheeks
and they begin to sweat.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:10.210
You ask what’s wrong, and your supervisor
murmurs one brief sentence.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:13.620
“You just met the most powerful person in
the world.”

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.560
Of course, you’ve heard of the O5 Council.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.850
They’re the most powerful people in the
entire SCP Foundation, both in terms of institutional

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.070
control, and perhaps even literal raw power.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:29.300
Depending on who you ask, they may be a group
of elite Foundation agents and researchers

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:34.910
who rose to the very top of the pyramid, a
secret room full of dusty, old power-hungry

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:40.790
bureaucrats, or a cabal of super-powered beings
that transcend the bounds of our dimension.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.880
In short, almost nobody is more powerful than
the Foundation’s O5 Council.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.660
But who Oversees the Overseers, if anyone
at all?

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.791
If they do exist, then who’s the one figure
in Foundation lore more secret than the most

00:02:54.791 --> 00:02:56.390
secretive group imaginable?

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:03.920
There’s only one answer to this question:
A figure known only as...The Administrator.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:08.810
If you spend enough time researching the affairs
of the SCP Foundation, there’s no doubt

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:13.760
you would have heard the name - perhaps in
a heavily-redacted file, or whispered in fear

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.120
by a Site Director worrying about incurring
the mysterious figure’s wrath.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:23.010
Today, we intend to do the impossible, and
we just might end up terminated by the Red

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.680
Right Hand because of it, but we’re going
to gather all the information available to

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:34.040
us, and try to figure out who or what the
clandestine Administrator actually is.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:39.290
We’ll answer your most obvious question
first: What’s with those weird, sandwich-stealing

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.290
arms?

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.460
One of the few almost universally-accepted
facts about the Administrator is their possession

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.900
of SCP-262, also known as the Coat of Many
Arms.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.010
Little to nothing is known about the coat’s
history before it came into the Administrator’s

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:59.620
possession, and given the huge amount of power
the Administrator wields within the Foundation,

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:03.130
nobody has the authority to press them for
further information.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:07.980
The coat’s interior is a spatial anomaly,
from which a huge number of anomalous limbs

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.280
can emerge and perform tasks on the wearer’s
behalf.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.250
It’s such a useful item that the Foundation
has even considered weaponizing it for field

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:21.139
agents, as the arms emerging from the coat
are able to perform tasks as diverse as playing

00:04:21.139 --> 00:04:26.360
the piano with two or more hands, to blocking
attacks directed towards the wearer that otherwise

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.740
would have been fatal.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:32.919
The limbs themselves are also varied, from
normal-looking human limbs to tentacles and

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:34.039
paws.

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:37.900
The Administrator only finally surrendered
the coat to the Foundation in the end because

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.639
it was taking up too much space in their closet,
and they presumably needed the room for the

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:46.219
next season’s most fashionable anomalous
clothing.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:50.729
For centuries though, you wouldn’t see the
Administrator without the many armed coat.

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:53.550
That’s right, centuries.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:58.180
Another almost universally-accepted fact about
the Administrator is that they have truly

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:02.539
freakish longevity, potentially living for
hundreds of years.

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:08.199
There has likely been more than one Administrator
during the Foundation’s extremely long history,

00:05:08.199 --> 00:05:11.599
but each one has survived longer than any
average human.

00:05:11.599 --> 00:05:15.680
It’s also a widely believed theory that
the Administrator may have been a key player

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.659
in the Foundation’s initial creation, too.

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:22.909
There’s been a number of potential names
speculated for the Administrator, including

00:05:22.909 --> 00:05:29.340
Frederick Williams, Agnes Peterson, Kismet,
and the sinister alias, The Spider.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:34.569
Some believe the Administrator to be fundamentally
human, despite certain anomalous qualities,

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:38.139
while others speculate that they’re the
furthest thing from human.

00:05:38.139 --> 00:05:43.029
This interpretation maintains that the Administrator
is an entity from a different dimension known

00:05:43.029 --> 00:05:48.569
as “The Plane Where Eyes Can’t Follow”,
and has a freakish body made from a twisted

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:54.139
charcoal-like material, tangled with wire
mesh and a chaos of different limbs - all

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:57.930
hidden under SCP-262.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:02.129
But hey, the Administrator’s species isn’t
nearly as interesting as their potential role

00:06:02.129 --> 00:06:07.050
within the Foundation, an issue surrounded
with nearly as much confusion and controversy

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.710
as...well, everything else about them.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:15.330
And just like everything else with the SCP
Foundation, the line they feed the public

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.879
is often different to the words circulating
within the Foundation’s higher clearance

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:20.879
levels.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:24.849
If you want to believe the official stories,
then the Administrator is the liaison between

00:06:24.849 --> 00:06:29.330
the Foundation and the numerous world governments
that need to cooperate with them to ensure

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.860
the successful capture of anomalies.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:37.220
The Administrator is only allowed to edit
SCP Files, not actually write them, due to

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:39.860
apparent “conflicts of interest.”

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:45.779
In many ways, the Administrator is presented
as your typical sleazy Washington insider:

00:06:45.779 --> 00:06:50.050
Schmoozing with politicians and government
figures to make sure they remain sympathetic

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.539
to the Foundation’s cause.

00:06:52.539 --> 00:06:56.379
According to observations from people outside
the Foundation who’ve worked with the mysterious

00:06:56.379 --> 00:07:03.180
figure, they have a penchant for finely tailored
suits, expensive aged liquors, and the amorous

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.020
company of women.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:09.099
Despite being a bit of a drunken horndog,
though, people tend to describe the Administrator

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:14.879
as likable and easy to get along with, regardless
of where you fall on the political spectrum.

00:07:14.879 --> 00:07:19.969
They’re also respected by many, and whenever
something upsets them, even powerful world

00:07:19.969 --> 00:07:22.759
leaders are eager to try and appease them.

00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:26.819
Maybe because they are described as being
freakishly strong when the situation demands

00:07:26.819 --> 00:07:27.819
it.

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:32.129
Hey, even world leaders can change their minds
when they have their arms twisted, literally.

00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:36.990
While there’s nothing too outwardly bizarre
about this iteration of the Administrator,

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:41.849
we don’t actually know how much of this
is true, a fact that really shouldn’t surprise

00:07:41.849 --> 00:07:43.099
you by now.

00:07:43.099 --> 00:07:48.940
And if being well-versed in the world of SCPs
has taught you anything, it’s that the SCP

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:52.969
Foundation’s PR and disinformation teams
are not to be trusted.

00:07:52.969 --> 00:07:55.009
So who can be trusted?

00:07:55.009 --> 00:07:59.589
Is there any perspective on this mysterious
figure that can be taken reliably?

00:07:59.589 --> 00:08:06.349
The short answer is… no, not really, but
we do have the next best thing: Recollections

00:08:06.349 --> 00:08:10.969
from some of the Foundation’s most trusted
researchers and personnel, and even some of

00:08:10.969 --> 00:08:16.119
the strange historical figures that have heard
about or even run into the administrator.

00:08:16.119 --> 00:08:21.199
What follows are some of their answers to
the question, “Who is the Administrator?”

00:08:21.199 --> 00:08:25.879
Professor Kain Pathos Crow said, “Oh, he’s
just something people talk about over lunch

00:08:25.879 --> 00:08:27.940
or when they’re between assignments.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:33.160
It kills time, and it’s a fun game to speculate
on who really calls the shots in this crazy

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:34.160
world.”

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.020
Field Agent Fritz Willie said, “I like to
tell people he’s my brother.”

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:41.530
Foundation Researcher Dr. Snorlison said,
“I’d like to poke at him and see what

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.530
happens.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:47.030
Just to see if any of the rumors about being
made entirely of legs and toes are true.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:49.340
Or something like that, at least.”

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:52.230
Director Neil Ghost said, “No big deal,
son.”

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.000
The ever-stoic Dr. Charles Gears said, “There
are no records of anyone by that name working

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.450
for the Foundation.”

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.500
Dr. Iceberg said, “Whatever the bossman
said goes.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.270
I’m not on staff to care about last decade’s
rumors.”

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:06.520
Dr. Glass said, “Never met the guy.

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:07.880
Heard he’s pretty interesting, though.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.960
I’d love to sit down and have a chat with
him, but he’s probably too busy.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.040
I’ve never even gotten a call back about
it.”

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.760
The wildcard Dr. Alto Clef said, “Who?”

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:19.690
Dr. Chelsea Elliott said, “I’ve actually
done some research on him.

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:24.010
Earliest records are about sixty years ago,
and beyond that there's some vague references

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:25.650
to a 'leader'.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:29.150
Most of the records, though, are incomplete
or just references by name.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.330
Not much of substance.”

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:33.580
Dr. Frederick Heiden said, “Please, leave
me alone.”

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.280
Dr. Jack Bright said, “Yeah, I’ve heard
of the guy yer talking about.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.380
He’s just a legendary thing, from back in
the day.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.980
When we thought there were twelve O5's, we
said he was there t'be the tie-breaker.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.730
People don’t talk about it much now, anymore.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:48.200
Probably because we don’t need icons like
that to keep people together.”

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:53.340
Dr. Jacob Kensington said, “I think he bought
me lunch once.”

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:57.460
Dr. Rights said, “I heard he lives up in
a biiiig tower at Overwatch, and he watches

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:01.900
down on the O5’s from the back of a mighty,
scaled dragon, and he flies the skies for

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:02.900
free!

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:04.630
Or, uh, something like that.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.240
You’ll have to wait until I finish the book
to hear the whole story.”

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.390
Dr. Kondraki said…

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:13.340
well we can’t tell you exactly what he said,
but it was short and to the point and he was

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.500
later disciplined for his use of rather rude
language.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:21.990
In an interview later suppressed by the SCP
Foundation, acclaimed horror writer Stephen

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:27.050
King said of his interaction with The Administrator,
“One of the oddest things to happen to me,

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.150
out on the road, was at an autograph session.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:30.820
In Westbrook, I think.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:34.350
A larger gentleman approached the table with
a copy of the Stand.

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:35.390
Said he was a big fan.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:38.970
Now, I think I might be a little crazy here,
but when I looked at his hand holding the

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.400
book, it was green.

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:43.500
I asked if he was okay, and I looked up into
his eyes.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:44.810
They were green too.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:45.990
He said he was fine.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.570
It was pretty scary stuff.”

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:53.570
Dr. Tilda D. Moose said, “No, no, I don’t
think we even humor that one anymore.

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:57.660
It’s like the mid-tier research staff telling
the new people there’s a pool on the third

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:58.660
floor.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:03.060
Nobody really believes it, but a couple people
every year try and ask, ‘just to check’.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:06.220
But yes, it’s a more or less dead rumor.”

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:09.230
And Dr. Django Bridge said, “Sure, I know
him.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.500
He hangs out at the pool on the fifth floor.”

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:16.550
So we return to our original question: Who
is The Administrator?

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:19.800
Do they rule the SCP Foundation, or serve
it?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.990
Are they an anomalous human, or a straight-up
monster?

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:27.570
Are they a liquor-loving political schmoozer
greasing the palms of the world’s government,

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:31.960
or a mysterious demi-god who founded the Foundation
and guides it on its quest to contain the

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.480
anomalous and protect normality?

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:39.610
The fact is, we don’t know, and thanks to
Foundation misinformation campaigns, we may

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:40.610
never know.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:46.010
But much like the Anti-Meme, The Administrator
is defined as much by what we don’t know

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.570
as what we do.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:51.500
And according to all sources, that’s exactly
how they like it.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.780
But what do you think is the truth about The
Administrator?

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:58.350
Just who exactly is lurking under that coat,
if anyone at all!

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:03.240
Let us know in the comments and then go check
out “Secret Group that Runs the World - SCP

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:08.940
O5 Council Explained” and “SCP Most Dangerous
Secret Labs and Facilities” for more of

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:12.440
the SCP Foundation’s most closely-held secrets!

